<title>FRANCE: SocGen sees no merger with big French bank.</title>
<headline>SocGen sees no merger with big French bank.</headline>
<dateline>PARIS 1997-05-13</dateline>
<text>
<p>Marc Vienot, chairman of French bank Societe Generale, said on Tuesday he did not see the bank merging with another bank that has a major French network.</p>
<p>&quot;A merger with another big bank with a French network is excluded, I think,&quot; he told an annual meeting of shareholders.</p>
<p>He did not think the massive job cuts that often result from mergers would be possible in France.</p>
<p>&quot;You cannot pull off that kind of operation in the French context,&quot; Vienot said.</p>
<p>-- Paris Newsroom +331 4221 5452</p>
</text>
